      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T14:29:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we want to be able to define this on a per cache basis so that if the data in a specific cache changes, it can be bumped?",
      "revId": "8297d180dc80a9ce1f50cd94b4c70850487dacca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e735a45_7080e374",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/cache/h2/H2CacheFactory.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T15:35:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is meant to cope with breaking changes in how h2 persists databases, not in changes how we serialize the data to be stored in them.\n\nHere h2 2.x cannot read/write databases which have been written using h2 1.x no matter which data is persistend in those databases.",
      "parentUuid": "c23375b3_ebfc05e4",
      "revId": "8297d180dc80a9ce1f50cd94b4c70850487dacca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9a853ff_7e2cd23f",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/cache/h2/H2CacheFactory.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T15:54:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m happy to have this either way, and it is easy enough to modify the code in the future if we want to do more with this, but is there any reason we would not want to bump this version if we make any sort of backward incompatible change to the contents of a cache also?",
      "parentUuid": "8e735a45_7080e374",
      "revId": "8297d180dc80a9ce1f50cd94b4c70850487dacca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "412300b9_6b69a984",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/cache/h2/H2CacheFactory.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T17:18:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "isn\u0027t that the purpose of the version set when CacheModule [creates a PersistentCacheProvider](https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/heads/master/java/com/google/gerrit/server/cache/CacheModule.java#165) ?",
      "parentUuid": "f9a853ff_7e2cd23f",
      "revId": "8297d180dc80a9ce1f50cd94b4c70850487dacca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6b9d48c5_b5141511",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/cache/h2/H2CacheFactory.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T00:54:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It does seem like it. We used to delete caches in init, now that is optional. I don\u0027t find any mention in the release notes of the need to force delete some caches, but I thought we used to have to. If we find that we have to in the future, I would advise that we consider bumping this number again.",
      "parentUuid": "412300b9_6b69a984",
      "revId": "8297d180dc80a9ce1f50cd94b4c70850487dacca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    }
